  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Electronic configuration of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Mn</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>25</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mi>Ar</mi></mfenced><mn>3</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mn>5</mn></msup><mn>4</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo></math> Electronic configuration of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Mn</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mi>Ar</mi></mfenced><mn>3</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math></p><p>Thus, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Mn</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math> has <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math>-unpaired electron and its spin only magnetic moment <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#956;</mi></mfenced></math> is, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#956;</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></msqrt></math> <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>BM</mi></math></p><p>where, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>=</mo></math> number of unpaired electrons.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#956;</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>3</mn><mo>(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo></msqrt><mo>.</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>BM</mi><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#956;</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>15</mn></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>87</mn><mi>BM</mi><mo>&#8776;</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>BM</mi></math></p>"
